		{"id":"5106ba62689e75bb","x":-442,"y":-297,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"[[Sturingaurd.canvas]]\n#PlayerCharacter "},
		{"id":"5801373d03155b6a","x":-380,"y":-160,"width":705,"height":430,"type":"text","text":"Stu\nNortheast of the Volstarian dynasty lies Thundercrest village, home to half-giants of the storm. I am the son of Guldar, the leader of Thundercrest. As a boy I was always stronger than the other children, often picking fights, I was known as a mindless brute. At 26 years old my father cast me out for my idiocy, told me strength can only get you so far in life and to come back a new man, stronger in both mind and body. And so I walked alone on the road through countless trials fighting bears and eating them to stay alive until one day, I saw a human boy being attacked by a pack of wolves. That day, everything in my mind changed. I had to keep this boy alive. After saving his life, he told me that his parents live in Volstar, the capital city of the Volstarian dynasty and apparently they were attacked by bandits on the road and they were separated. And so began their 3 month long journey. As I walked and carried Basil on my shoulders, I felt a deep connection forming and began to look at him as a younger brother. Eventually we reached the capital city and I dropped Basil off at his house. His parents were forever grateful and told me that they knew of a group of people that I could trust to use my strength for good and truly see the world. Now those idiots on a stupid job got me stuck in this fucking shithole.\n"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}